//   - "select min ( weight ) from cars_data where cylinders = 8 and year = 1974"
//
// The correct answers USE table.column notation AND use JOINs!
// Our guidance is saying NEVER use table.column, but the correct answers DO use it.
// This is likely causing failures for queries that NEED table.column references.
//
// New theory: The guidance "Never use table.column notation" is HURTING accuracy because
// many correct answers do use table.column (like "employee.name").
// Meanwhile "Never use AS aliases" might be fine (correct answers don't use aliases).
