//   - Allow table.column notation for ON clauses in JOINs
//   - Disallow bare table aliases (no "FROM flights f" or "f.column")
//   - Focus on JOIN structure: use explicit ON conditions
//   - Discourage overly complex queries with many JOINs when simple WHERE works
//
// Better guidance: "Use proper SQL syntax. Use explicit JOIN ... ON ... syntax.
//   Do not use short table aliases (no 'FROM table t' - write the full table name).
//   For max/min use ORDER BY col DESC/ASC LIMIT 1 when appropriate.
//   Reference columns by table.column when joining multiple tables.
//   Keep queries direct and simple - avoid unnecessary subqueries."
